readings.text:
[Deuteronomy 11:1] “And you shall love <dn>את</dn> <dn>YeHoVaH</dn> your <dn>Elohim</dn> and guard <dn>His</dn> charge: even <dn>His</dn> laws, and <dn>His</dn> right-rulings, and <dn>His</dn> commands, always.
[2] “And you shall know today – for it is not <dn>את</dn> your children who have not known and who have not seen <dn>את</dn> the discipline of <dn>YeHoVaH</dn> your <dn>Elohim</dn>, <dn>את</dn> <dn>His</dn> greatness, <dn>את</dn> <dn>His</dn> strong hand and <dn>His</dn> outstretched arm,
[3] and <dn>את</dn> <dn>His</dn> signs, and <dn>את</dn> <dn>His</dn> works which <dn>He</dn> had done in the midst of Mitsrayim, to Pharaoh sovereign of Mitsrayim, and to all his land;
[4] and that which <dn>He</dn> had done to the army of Mitsrayim, to their horses and their chariots, when <dn>He</dn> made <dn>את</dn> the waters of the Sea of Reeds overflow them as they pursued you, and how <dn>YeHoVaH</dn> has destroyed them to this day;
[5] and what <dn>He</dn> had done for you in the wilderness till you came to this place;
[6] and what <dn>He</dn> had done to Dathan and Aḇiram the sons of Eliyaḇ, son of Re’uḇěn, when the earth opened <dn>את</dn> its mouth and swallowed them up, and <dn>את</dn> their households, and <dn>את</dn> their tents, and <dn>את</dn> all the living creatures that were in their possession, in the midst of all Yisra’ěl.
[7] “For yours are the eyes that saw <dn>את</dn> all the great work of <dn>YeHoVaH</dn>, which <dn>He</dn> did.
